meta {
  name: Validate Credentials
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/employees
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Validate Factorial credentials

  A single read request used to confirm the API key + base URL are valid
  before building out the integration.

  ## How to use

  1. Open this folder as a collection in Bruno.
  2. Select the **Sandbox** environment (top-right).
  3. Set the secret `apiKey` variable to your Factorial API key
     (Environment settings -> Sandbox -> apiKey). It is stored locally,
     not committed.
  4. Send the request.

  ## Expected

  - **200 OK** with a JSON body containing a `data` array of employees
    -> credentials are valid.
  - **401 / 403** -> the key is wrong, expired, or lacks the scope to
    read employees.

  ## Notes

  - Auth: Factorial API keys are sent as the `x-api-key` header
    (confirmed against the API docs), value is the raw key with no prefix.
  - Base URLs: sandbox `https://api.eu2.demo.factorial.dev`,
    production `https://api.factorialhr.com`.
}
